{
  "summary": "Permits running -txindex concurrently with block pruning (-prune) as long as the index does not contain legacy file-offset entries. When a transaction lookup via txindex or GetTransaction targets a block that has been pruned from disk, the lookup returns candidate pruned block hashes. RPC calls (getrawtransaction, gettxoutproof) and the REST /tx endpoint return structured error information containing those block hashes so callers can fetch the missing blocks on demand via getblockfrompeer.",
  "problem": "Running txindex has historically been blocked on pruned nodes because legacy index entries stored direct file positions on disk. Pruned node operators could not use txindex to locate transactions or service RPC lookups like getrawtransaction without storing the full blockchain on disk.",
  "evidence": [
    "Resolves four long-standing issues requesting txindex support on pruned nodes dating back to 2017: #10609, #12651, #16182, and #35240 (PR description)."
  ],
